NOTICE OF MODIFICATIONS

This software is a derivative work of Triangle Version 1.6 by Jonathan
Richard Shewchuk.  The original C sources (triangle.c, triangle.h) were
completely rewritten (ported) in the Rust programming language.  In
accordance with the license above, this port and all modifications made
to the original code remain under copyright of the original author, and
both source and object code are made freely available without charge.

Summary of modifications:

  * Complete rewrite of Triangle from C to Rust.
  * The original program API (triangle.h / triangulate()) was replaced by
    a Rust library API.
  * Command line interface and feature set may differ from the original
    Triangle; see README.md for details.
  * The original single-file C structure was replaced by a Rust crate
    and module layout.

The original C sources and documentation are available from the Triangle
Web page:

    http://www.cs.cmu.edu/~quake/triangle.html

Bug reports and comments regarding this Rust port should be directed to
the issue tracker of this project's repository, not to the original
author.  
Bug reports regarding the original C version of Triangle remain
welcome at jrs@cs.berkeley.edu.

If you use a mesh generated by this software in a publication, please
acknowledge Triangle as described in the original documentation:

    Jonathan Richard Shewchuk, "Triangle: Engineering a 2D Quality Mesh
    Generator and Delaunay Triangulator," in Applied Computational
    Geometry: Towards Geometric Engineering (Ming C. Lin and Dinesh
    Manocha, editors), volume 1148 of Lecture Notes in Computer Science,
    pages 203-222, Springer-Verlag, Berlin, May 1996.  (From the First
    ACM Workshop on Applied Computational Geometry.)
